---
layout: default
page_class: "course webinar selling"
title: "When the Cloud Savings Stop"
description: "Why the finance playbook stops finding money, and the architecture decisions that set your cloud bill."
image: /images/sales/architecting-for-cost/og.png
# Supporting page (Spec0031 §B5), same pattern as architecting-with-ai.erb.
# `state` is upcoming or replay. Live even before the LinkedIn Event exists
# (Lee, 2026-10-03): with `linkedin_event_url` blank, the page says that
# registration opens soon instead of showing the button.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER MOVE OR RENAME THIS FILE. The short link /cost-webinar (a 302 in
# netlify.toml) points at /webinars/architecting-for-cost/, and that short
# link is spoken in a recorded video and shown on its last slide.
state: upcoming
starts_at: "Thursday, November 19, 10am Pacific"
linkedin_event_url: ""          # the LinkedIn Event; blank shows "registration opens soon"
replay_url: ""                  # set when state: replay
# The replay page links to this offer while it is active, else to the
# product's sales page.
product: architecting-for-cost
offer_slug: launch
---

<%
  unless %w[upcoming replay].include?(data.state)
    raise "#{resource.relative_path}: state: #{data.state} must be upcoming or replay"
  end
  course_url = relative_url current_offer_url(data.product, data.offer_slug)
%>

<%# Title and one-line description: Lee, 2026-10-02. %>
<section class="course-header">
  <div class="course-header-inner">
    <div class="course-badge-row">
      <span class="course-platform-badge">Free Webinar</span>
      <span class="course-stat-line"><%= data.state == "replay" ? "Replay" : data.starts_at %></span>
    </div>
    <h1><%= data.title %></h1>
    <p class="webinar-lead">Why the finance playbook stops finding money, and the architecture decisions that set your cloud bill.</p>
    <div class="webinar-actions">
      <% if data.state == "upcoming" %>
        <% if data.linkedin_event_url.to_s != "" %>
          <%# LinkedIn is third-party, so it opens in a new tab. %>
          <a href="<%= data.linkedin_event_url %>" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Register on LinkedIn &rarr;</a>
        <% else %>
          <p class="webinar-pending">Registration opens soon on LinkedIn. Check back here for the link.</p>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <% if data.replay_url.to_s != "" %>
          <a href="<%= data.replay_url %>" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch the Replay &rarr;</a>
        <% end %>
        <a href="<%= course_url %>" class="btn btn-outline">See the course &rarr;</a>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="course-body">
  <div class="course-body-inner">
    <% if data.state == "upcoming" %>
      <% if data.linkedin_event_url.to_s != "" %>
        <p>A free 30-minute webinar on <%= data.starts_at %>. Register through the LinkedIn Event.</p>
      <% else %>
        <p>A free 30-minute webinar on <%= data.starts_at %>. Registration opens soon on LinkedIn, and the link will be on this page.</p>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <p>The replay is free. The webinar is the premise of the course <a href="<%= course_url %>">Architecting for Cost</a>.</p>
    <% end %>

    <%# The same in every run and both states (Lee, 2026-10-03). Both links
        open a new tab (Lee's call), so a viewer doesn't lose this page. %>
    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>Want to ask me something? Send me a note through <a href="https://leeatchison.com/contact" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">my contact form</a>, or reach me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leeatchison/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
